@startuml test-e2e-topology
!include style.iuml

title Container end-to-end and contract topology (L4, L5)

node "CI runner or developer machine (Docker)" {
  node "compose network: e2e" {
    node "bridge\nimage built from Dockerfile" as bridge
    node "donetick-stub\nWireMock.Net image,\nsame mappings as L2" as stub
    node "donetick-real\ndonetick image + SQLite,\npinned version" as real
    node "e2e-runner\npytest + caldav library" as runner
    folder "certs\nself-signed, test only" as certs
  }
}

runner --> bridge : CalDAV over HTTPS\n(Basic auth)
bridge --> stub : eAPI\n(profile: stub)
bridge ..> real : eAPI\n(profile: contract)
runner ..> stub : admin API:\nseed and verify
runner ..> real : eAPI:\nseed and verify
bridge ..> certs : mounted read-only

note right of real
  Contract profile only.
  Open question: provisioning
  a user and an API key
  automatically.
end note

note bottom of runner
  Also checks container behaviour:
  health endpoint, restart rebuilds the cache,
  invalid configuration exits non-zero.
end note
@enduml
